IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spc-nouns`

-- State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- LAYER 1, "Interpretation of state pension
-- credit provisions" (sections 15, 16 and 17).
--
-- It comes before the Parts that use it because the stable l4 resolves IMPORT in
-- one direction only: the entitlement module imports this one. Section 17(1)'s
-- definition of "entitled" calls sections 1 to 5, so it sits at the foot of the
-- entitlement module, not here (see spc-part-entitlement.l4).
--
-- Layer 1 takes nobody's point of view. A rule here states a relation or a test
-- once, in the Act's own words, and is called by the seat layer; it is never
-- copied there.

§ `Interpretation of state pension credit provisions`

§§ `15 Income and capital`

-- Section 15(1): "income" is income of ten descriptions. The Income record
-- holds one amount for each, in the Act's order, so the Act's definition is the
-- sum of its ten limbs. (Written as `sum` over a LIST, not as ten PLUSes: on the
-- stable l4 a left-nested chain of ten PLUS took 27 seconds to check, and this
-- takes under one. See NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept".)
-- src:202 | (1) In this Act “income” means income of any of the following descriptions—
-- src:203 | (a) earnings;
-- src:204 | (b) working tax credit;
-- src:205 | (c) retirement pension income;
-- src:206 | (d) income from annuity contracts (other than retirement pension income);
-- src:207 | (e) prescribed social security benefits (other than retirement pension income and state pension credit);
-- src:208 | (f) foreign social security benefits of any prescribed description;
-- src:209 | (g) a war disablement pension or war widow’s or widower’s pension;
-- src:210 | (h) a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow’s or widower’s pension;
-- src:211 | (i) income from capital;
-- src:212 | (j) income of any prescribed description.
@ref s 15(1) (src:202-212)
GIVEN income IS AN Income
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 15(1) -- income` income MEANS
    sum (LIST
        income's earnings,
        income's `working tax credit`,
        income's `retirement pension income`,
        income's `income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension income`,
        income's `prescribed social security benefits other than retirement pension income and state pension credit`,
        income's `foreign social security benefits of a prescribed description`,
        income's `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension`,
        income's `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension`,
        income's `income from capital`,
        income's `income of a prescribed description` )

-- Section 15(2): regulations MAY deem capital to yield income at a prescribed
-- rate. Whether they do, and at what rate, are not in the inputs: both are inputs.
-- src:213 | (2) Regulations may provide that a person’s capital shall be deemed to yield him income at a prescribed rate.
@ref s 15(2) (src:213)
GIVEN capital IS A NUMBER
      `regulations deem capital to yield income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 15(2) -- income deemed to be yielded by capital` capital `regulations deem capital to yield income` `prescribed rate` MEANS
    IF `regulations deem capital to yield income`
    THEN capital TIMES `prescribed rate`
    ELSE 0

-- Section 15(3) to (7) (how income and capital are calculated or estimated; the
-- averaging rules; the circumstances in which a person is treated as having, or
-- as not having, capital or income; income treated as capital and capital as
-- income): every one is a power to make regulations and the Act states no figure
-- or rule in them. They are INERT in layer 1. Their only effect is on the amounts
-- the Income record carries, which are "income as the prescribed rules calculate
-- it" by construction (see spc-nouns.l4).
-- src:214 | (3) Income and capital shall be calculated or estimated in such manner as may be prescribed.
-- src:215 | (4) A person’s income in respect of any period shall be calculated in accordance with prescribed rules.
-- src:216 | (5) The rules may provide for the calculation to be made by reference to an average over a period (which need not consist of or include the whole or any part of the period concerned).
-- src:217 | (6) Circumstances may be prescribed in which—
-- src:218 | (a) a person is treated as possessing capital or income which he does not possess;
-- src:219 | (b) capital or income which a person does possess is to be disregarded;
-- src:220 | (c) income is to be treated as capital; or
-- src:221 | (d) capital is to be treated as income.
-- src:222 | (7) Subsections (2) to (6) have effect for the purposes of this Act.
-- (not encoded: section 15(3) to (7) are regulation-making powers)

§§ `16 Retirement pension income`

-- Section 16(1) lists the descriptions of "retirement pension income", and
-- section 7(6) (assessed income periods) needs to tell some of them apart by the
-- Act under which they are paid (Great Britain or Northern Ireland). So each
-- description here is one constructor, taken from the Act's own list, and the
-- country of the law is a separate fact.
--
-- This one type also carries the other descriptions of income in section 15(1),
-- so that "what description is this income?" is one question with one answer.
DECLARE `Description of income` IS ONE OF
    earnings                                                                          -- s 15(1)(a)
    `working tax credit`                                                              -- s 15(1)(b)
    -- s 15(1)(c) retirement pension income, by the paragraphs of section 16(1):
    `a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or its Northern Ireland counterpart`  -- (za)
    `a Category A or Category B retirement pension`                                   -- (a)
    `a shared additional pension`                                                     -- (b)
    `graduated retirement benefit`                                                    -- (c)
    `a Category C or Category D retirement pension`                                   -- (d)
    `age addition`                                                                    -- (e)
    `income from an occupational pension scheme or a personal pension scheme`         -- (f)
    `income from an overseas arrangement`                                             -- (g)
    `income from a retirement annuity contract`                                       -- (h)
    `income from annuities or insurance policies purchased or transferred to give effect to rights under a personal pension scheme or an overseas arrangement` -- (i)
    `income from annuities purchased or entered into to discharge liability for pension credits on divorce` -- (j)
    `a pension under section 5 of the Civil List Act 1837 or section 7 of the Civil List Act 1952` -- (k)
    `a payment by a former employer on account of early retirement on grounds of ill-health or disability` -- (l)
    `a payment at regular intervals under an equity release scheme`                   -- (m)
    `a payment under the Financial Assistance Scheme Regulations 2005`                -- (n)
    -- the other descriptions of section 15(1):
    `income from an annuity contract other than retirement pension income`            -- s 15(1)(d)
    `a prescribed social security benefit other than retirement pension income and state pension credit` -- s 15(1)(e)
    `a foreign social security benefit of a prescribed description`                   -- s 15(1)(f)
    `a war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension`                   -- s 15(1)(g)
    `a foreign war disablement pension or foreign war widow's or widower's pension`   -- s 15(1)(h)
    `income from capital`                                                             -- s 15(1)(i)
    `income of a prescribed description`                                              -- s 15(1)(j)
    `PPF periodic payments`                                                           -- named by section 7(6)(d); not listed in section 15(1)

-- Section 16(1): which descriptions are retirement pension income. Every
-- paragraph is a description, with one exclusion written into paragraph (l):
-- a payment "ordered by a court or made in settlement of a claim" is not one.
-- src:224 | (1) In this Act “retirement pension income” means any of the following—
-- src:225 | (za) a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or under any provision in Northern Ireland which corresponds to that Part;
-- src:226 | (a) a Category A or Category B retirement pension payable under sections 43 to 55 of—
-- src:227 | (i) the Contributions and Benefits Act; or
-- src:228 | (ii) the Social Security Contributions and Benefits (Northern Ireland) Act 1992 (c. 7);
-- src:229 | (b) a shared additional pension payable under—
-- src:230 | (i) section 55A of either of those Acts, or
-- src:231 | (ii) section 55AA of the Contributions and Benefits Act or any corresponding provision under the law of Northern Ireland;
-- src:232 | (c) graduated retirement benefit payable under section 62 of either of those Acts;
-- src:233 | (d) a Category C or Category D retirement pension payable under section 78 of either of those Acts;
-- src:234 | (e) age addition payable under section 79 of either of those Acts;
-- src:235 | (f) income from an occupational pension scheme or a personal pension scheme;
-- src:236 | (g) income from an overseas arrangement;
-- src:237 | (h) income from a retirement annuity contract;
-- src:238 | (i) income from annuities or insurance policies purchased or transferred for the purpose of giving effect to rights under a personal pension scheme or an overseas arrangement;
-- src:239 | (j) income from annuities purchased or entered into for the purpose of discharging liability under—
-- src:240 | (i) section 29(1)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999 (c. 30) (pension credits on divorce); or
-- src:241 | (ii) Article 26(1)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 1999 (S.I. 1999/3147 (N.I. 11)) (corresponding provision for Northern Ireland).
-- src:242 | (k) any sum payable by way of pension under section 5 of the Civil List Act 1837 or section 7 of the Civil List Act 1952;
-- src:243 | (l) any payment, other than a payment ordered by a court or made in settlement of a claim, made by or on behalf of a former employer of a person on account of the early retirement of that person on grounds of ill-health or disability
-- src:244 | (m) any payment made at regular intervals under an equity release scheme.
-- src:245 | (n) any payment made under the Financial Assistance Scheme Regulations 2005.
@ref s 16(1) (src:224-245)
GIVEN description IS A `Description of income`
      `ordered by a court or made in settlement of a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) -- retirement pension income` description `ordered by a court or made in settlement of a claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER description
        WHEN `a state pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 or its Northern Ireland counterpart` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a Category A or Category B retirement pension` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a shared additional pension` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `graduated retirement benefit` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a Category C or Category D retirement pension` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `age addition` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `income from an occupational pension scheme or a personal pension scheme` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `income from an overseas arrangement` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `income from a retirement annuity contract` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `income from annuities or insurance policies purchased or transferred to give effect to rights under a personal pension scheme or an overseas arrangement` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `income from annuities purchased or entered into to discharge liability for pension credits on divorce` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a pension under section 5 of the Civil List Act 1837 or section 7 of the Civil List Act 1952` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a payment by a former employer on account of early retirement on grounds of ill-health or disability` THEN NOT (`ordered by a court or made in settlement of a claim`)
        WHEN `a payment at regular intervals under an equity release scheme` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a payment under the Financial Assistance Scheme Regulations 2005` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Section 16(2): the Secretary of State may by regulations add to, vary or remove
-- the descriptions listed in 16(1). No such regulations are among the inputs, so
-- the list above is the list in the deposited text. INERT (a power).
-- src:246 | (2) The Secretary of State may by regulations amend subsection (1); and any such regulations may—
-- src:247 | (a) add to or vary the descriptions of income for the time being listed in that subsection; or
-- src:248 | (b) remove any such description from that subsection.
-- (not encoded: section 16(2) is a power to amend the list; none is among the inputs)

-- Section 16(3): "overseas arrangement" and "retirement annuity contract" take
-- their meanings from other Acts (the Pension Schemes Act 1993 section 181(1);
-- Chapter 3 of Part 14 of the Income and Corporation Taxes Act 1988), which are
-- not among the inputs. Borrowed terms: the person says whether a payment is
-- from one of them by choosing the description above.
-- src:249 | (3) In this section—
-- src:250 | “overseas arrangement” has the meaning given by section 181(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (c. 48);
-- src:251 | “retirement annuity contract” means a contract or scheme approved under Chapter 3 of Part 14 of the Income and Corporation Taxes Act 1988 (c. 1).
-- (not encoded: section 16(3) points at definitions in other Acts)

§§ `17 Other interpretation provisions`

-- Section 17(1) "couple": two limbs. (a) is married or civil partners AND in the
-- same household. (b) is NOT married or civil partners, but living together as a
-- married couple or civil partners, otherwise than in prescribed circumstances.
-- src:261 | “couple” means—
-- src:262 | (a) two people who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are members of the same household; or
-- src:263 | (b) two people who are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as a married couple as if they were a married couple or civil partners otherwise than in prescribed circumstances;
@ref s 17(1) "couple" (src:261-263)
GIVEN household IS A Household
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- couple` household MEANS
        (    household's `married to or civil partners of each other`
         AND household's `members of the same household` )
    OR  (    (NOT (household's `married to or civil partners of each other`))
         AND household's `living together as a married couple or as civil partners`
         AND (NOT (household's `in prescribed circumstances that take them outside paragraph (b)`)) )

-- Section 17(1) "foreign social security benefit": any benefit, allowance or other
-- payment paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom AND in the
-- nature of social security.
-- src:271 | “foreign social security benefit” means any benefit, allowance or other payment which is paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom and is in the nature of social security;
@ref s 17(1) "foreign social security benefit" (src:271)
GIVEN `paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the nature of social security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- foreign social security benefit` `paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom` `in the nature of social security` MEANS
        `paid under the law of a country outside the United Kingdom`
    AND `in the nature of social security`

-- Section 17(1) "foreign war disablement pension": granted by the government of
-- a country outside the UK, AND either (a) in respect of disablement arising from
-- forces' service or war injury, or (b) corresponding in nature to a retired pay
-- or pension to which section 641 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act
-- 2003 applies (that section is not among the inputs: paragraph (b) is a fact).
-- src:272 | “foreign war disablement pension” means any retired pay, pension, allowance or similar payment granted by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom—
-- src:273 | (a) in respect of disablement arising from forces’ service or war injury; or
-- src:274 | (b) corresponding in nature to any retired pay or pension to which section 641 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies;
@ref s 17(1) "foreign war disablement pension" (src:272-274)
GIVEN `granted by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in respect of disablement arising from forces' service or war injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `corresponding in nature to a retired pay or pension to which section 641 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- foreign war disablement pension` `granted by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom` `in respect of disablement arising from forces' service or war injury` `corresponding in nature to a retired pay or pension to which section 641 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies` MEANS
        `granted by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom`
    AND (   `in respect of disablement arising from forces' service or war injury`
         OR `corresponding in nature to a retired pay or pension to which section 641 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies` )

-- Section 17(1) "foreign war widow's or widower's pension": the same shape for a
-- widow, widower or surviving civil partner and a death due to forces' service or
-- war injury, or a pension corresponding in nature to one under section 641(1)(e) or (f).
-- src:275 | “foreign war widow’s or widower’s pension” means any pension, allowance or similar payment granted to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom—
-- src:276 | (a) in respect of a death due to forces’ service or war injury; or
-- src:277 | (b) corresponding in nature to a pension or allowance for a widow, widower or surviving civil partner under any scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003;
@ref s 17(1) "foreign war widow's or widower's pension" (src:275-277)
GIVEN `granted to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in respect of a death due to forces' service or war injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `corresponding in nature to a pension or allowance under a scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- foreign war widow's or widower's pension` `granted to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom` `in respect of a death due to forces' service or war injury` `corresponding in nature to a pension or allowance under a scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` MEANS
        `granted to a widow, widower or surviving civil partner by the government of a country outside the United Kingdom`
    AND (   `in respect of a death due to forces' service or war injury`
         OR `corresponding in nature to a pension or allowance under a scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` )

-- Section 17(1) "war disablement pension": (a) retired pay, pension or allowance
-- granted in respect of disablement under powers conferred by or under one of the
-- five Acts the paragraph lists, or (b), without prejudice to (a), a retired pay
-- or pension to which any of paragraphs (a) to (f) of section 641(1) of the Income
-- Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies (not among the inputs: a fact).
-- src:298 | “war disablement pension” means—
-- src:299 | (a) any retired pay, pension or allowance granted in respect of disablement under powers conferred by or under—
-- src:300 | (i) the Air Force (Constitution) Act 1917 (c. 51);
-- src:301 | (ii) the Personal Injuries (Emergency Provisions) Act 1939 (c. 82);
-- src:302 | (iii) the Pensions (Navy, Army, Air Force and Mercantile Marine) Act 1939 (c. 83);
-- src:303 | (iv) the Polish Resettlement Act 1947 (c. 19); or
-- src:304 | (v) Part 7 or section 151 of the Reserve Forces Act 1980 (c. 9); or
-- src:305 | (b) without prejudice to paragraph (a), any retired pay or pension to which any of paragraphs (a) to (f) of section 641(1) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies;
@ref s 17(1) "war disablement pension" (src:298-305)
GIVEN `granted in respect of disablement under powers conferred by or under one of the Acts in paragraph (a)(i) to (v)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a retired pay or pension to which any of paragraphs (a) to (f) of section 641(1) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- war disablement pension` `granted in respect of disablement under powers conferred by or under one of the Acts in paragraph (a)(i) to (v)` `a retired pay or pension to which any of paragraphs (a) to (f) of section 641(1) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies` MEANS
        `granted in respect of disablement under powers conferred by or under one of the Acts in paragraph (a)(i) to (v)`
    OR  `a retired pay or pension to which any of paragraphs (a) to (f) of section 641(1) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 applies`

-- Section 17(1) "war widow's or widower's pension": (a) a widow's, widower's or
-- surviving civil partner's pension or allowance granted in respect of a death due
-- to service or war injury and payable by virtue of an enactment named in the
-- definition of "war disablement pension" paragraph (a), or (b) a pension or
-- allowance granted under a scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f).
-- src:306 | “war widow’s or widower’s pension” means—
-- src:307 | (a) any widow's, widower’s or surviving civil partner's pension or allowance granted in respect of a death due to service or war injury and payable by virtue of any enactment mentioned in paragraph (a) of the definition of “war disablement pension”; or
-- src:308 | (b) a pension or allowance for a widow, widower or surviving civil partner granted under any scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003;
@ref s 17(1) "war widow's or widower's pension" (src:306-308)
GIVEN `granted in respect of a death due to service or war injury and payable by virtue of an enactment mentioned in paragraph (a) of the definition of war disablement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `granted under a scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- war widow's or widower's pension` `granted in respect of a death due to service or war injury and payable by virtue of an enactment mentioned in paragraph (a) of the definition of war disablement pension` `granted under a scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` MEANS
        `granted in respect of a death due to service or war injury and payable by virtue of an enactment mentioned in paragraph (a) of the definition of war disablement pension`
    OR  `granted under a scheme mentioned in section 641(1)(e) or (f) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003`

-- Section 17(1) "working tax credit": a working tax credit under the Tax Credits
-- Act 2002 to which a person is entitled, whether alone or jointly with another.
-- src:309 | “working tax credit” means a working tax credit under the Tax Credits Act 2002 to which a person is entitled whether alone or jointly with another.
@ref s 17(1) "working tax credit" (src:309)
GIVEN `a working tax credit under the Tax Credits Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to it, alone or jointly with another` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- working tax credit` `a working tax credit under the Tax Credits Act 2002` `the person is entitled to it, alone or jointly with another` MEANS
        `a working tax credit under the Tax Credits Act 2002`
    AND `the person is entitled to it, alone or jointly with another`

-- Section 17(1) "PPF periodic payments": (a) periodic compensation payments made
-- in relation to a person and payable under the pension compensation provisions
-- (section 162(2) of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 146(2) of the Pensions
-- (Northern Ireland) Order 2005); or (b) periodic payments payable under section 166
-- of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 150 of that Order.
-- src:286 | “PPF periodic payments” means—
-- src:287 | (a) any periodic compensation payments made in relation to a person, payable under the pension compensation provisions as specified in section 162(2) of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 146(2) of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005 (the pension compensation provisions); or
-- src:288 | (b) any periodic payments made in relation to a person, payable under section 166 of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 150 of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005 (duty to pay scheme benefits unpaid at assessment date etc.);
@ref s 17(1) "PPF periodic payments" (src:286-288)
GIVEN `periodic compensation payments payable under the pension compensation provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `periodic payments payable under section 166 of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 150 of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- PPF periodic payments` `periodic compensation payments payable under the pension compensation provisions` `periodic payments payable under section 166 of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 150 of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005` MEANS
        `periodic compensation payments payable under the pension compensation provisions`
    OR  `periodic payments payable under section 166 of the Pensions Act 2004 or Article 150 of the Pensions (Northern Ireland) Order 2005`

-- Section 17(1), every other entry. Each is one of: a pointer to the section
-- that defines the term ("assessed income period", "appropriate minimum
-- guarantee", "capital", "element", "guarantee credit", "income", "qualifying
-- age", "retirement pension income", "retirement provision", "savings credit",
-- "standard minimum guarantee" -- the rules for them are in the modules for the
-- sections named); a short name for another Act ("the Administration Act", "the
-- Contributions and Benefits Act"); a plain restatement ("claimant" means a
-- claimant for state pension credit; "prescribed" means specified in, or determined
-- in accordance with, regulations; "regulations" means regulations made by the
-- Secretary of State; "social security benefits" means benefits payable under the
-- enactments relating to social security in any part of the United Kingdom); or a
-- term defined by another Act that is not among the inputs ("earnings" -- Parts 1
-- to 5 of the Contributions and Benefits Act; "occupational pension scheme" and
-- "personal pension scheme" -- the Pension Schemes Acts 1993; "carer support
-- payment" -- the Carer's Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland)
-- Regulations 2023; "pensionable age" -- paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the
-- Pensions Act 1995). The borrowed terms are asked as facts. "entitled" is
-- encoded at the foot of spc-part-entitlement.l4, because it calls sections 1 to 5.
-- Lines 280, 297 and 310 of the deposited text are blank entries (". . ." / "...").
-- src:253 | (1) In this Act—
-- src:254 | “the Administration Act” means the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (c. 5);
-- src:255 | “assessed income period” shall be construed in accordance with sections 6 and 9;
-- src:256 | “appropriate minimum guarantee” shall be construed in accordance with section 2(3);
-- src:257 | “capital” shall be construed in accordance with section 15;
-- src:258 | “carer support payment” means the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023;
-- src:259 | “claimant” means a claimant for state pension credit;
-- src:260 | “the Contributions and Benefits Act” means the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (c. 4);
-- src:261 | “couple” means—
-- src:262 | (a) two people who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are members of the same household; or
-- src:263 | (b) two people who are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as a married couple as if they were a married couple or civil partners otherwise than in prescribed circumstances;
-- src:264 | “earnings” has the same meaning as in Parts 1 to 5 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (see sections 3(1) and 112, and the definition of “employment” in section 122, of that Act);
-- src:265 | “element”, in relation to the claimant’s retirement provision, shall be construed in accordance with section 7(6);
-- src:266 | “entitled”, in relation to state pension credit, shall be construed in accordance with—
-- src:267 | (a) this Act,
-- src:268 | (b) section 1 of the Administration Act (entitlement to be dependent on making of claim etc), and
-- src:269 | (c) section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998 (c. 14) (restrictions on entitlement to benefit in certain cases of error),
-- src:270 | (and, in relation to any other benefit within the meaning of section 1 of the Administration Act or section 27 of the Social Security Act 1998, in accordance with that section or (as the case may be) both of those sections in addition to any other conditions relating to that benefit);
-- (not encoded as separate rules: see the comment above)

-- Section 17(2): regulations may say when persons are treated as members of the
-- same household and as severely disabled. A power; INERT. Its outcomes are the
-- BOOLEAN facts `members of the same household` and `severely disabled`, which
-- the person states as the regulations treat them.
-- src:311 | (2) Regulations may make provision for the purposes of this Act—
-- src:312 | (a) as to circumstances in which persons are to be treated as being or not being members of the same household;
-- src:313 | (b) as to circumstances in which persons are to be treated as being or not being severely disabled.
-- (not encoded: section 17(2) is a power to make regulations)

-- Section 17(3): sections 172 and 173 of the Contributions and Benefits Act apply
-- (Great Britain and adjacent waters; the meaning of attaining an age). Not among
